# Feature: IPC bridge

## Transport

- Electron `child_process.spawn(python, ["-u", "{root}/python/main.py"], { stdio: pipe })`.
- `PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1`. `FIELDY_ROOT` + `FIELDY_YAMNET_DIR`.
- One JSON object per line on stdin/stdout.
- **stdout = protocol only.** All logs, TF warnings, traceback → stderr.

## Messages

```json
{"id": "1", "method": "classify_and_ingest", "params": {"paths": ["/abs/a.wav"]}}
{"id": "1", "ok": true, "result": {"jobs": []}}
{"id": "1", "ok": false, "error": "message"}
{"type": "event", "name": "progress", "payload": {"file": "a.wav", "stage": "analyze", "pct": 40, "fileIndex": 0, "fileCount": 1}}
```

## Methods

| method | params | result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ping | {} | {pong:true} |
| get_config | {} | config or {needsOnboarding:true}; may include `libraryRootProblem`: `missing` \| `unreadable` |
| save_config | {libraryRoot, thresholds…, playback prefs?, libraryRootMode?} | {ok:true} — merges with previous saved config. `libraryRootMode` is `relocate` or `fresh`. Playback keys: `playbackVolume` 0–1, `playbackLoop`, `autoPlayOnSelect`, `playbackMuted`, `playbackPitch`, `playbackPitchEnabled`, `playbackPitchRange` 2\|4\|8, `playbackPitchResetOnNew`, `playbackPreservePitch` |
| classify_and_ingest | {paths: string[]} | {jobs: JobResult[]} |
| list_library | {} | {libraryRoot, folders, recentlyAdded, favorites, collections} |
| move_file | {src or paths, destFolder} | {path, paths} — inside libraryRoot; destFolder is Mixed or an AudioSet class |
| rename_file | {path, newName} | {path} — basename only; extension kept if omitted |
| delete_file | {path or paths} | {ok:true} — file only, must be inside libraryRoot |
| set_favorite | {path or paths, favorite} | {path, paths, favorite} — persist per libraryRoot; not a disk folder |
| create_collection | {name} | {id, name} — virtual list, no mkdir |
| add_to_collection | {id, path or paths} | {id, path, paths} — library files |
| prepare_playback | {path} | {previewPath, duration, peaksMin, peaksMax, …} — 16-bit temp WAV + waveform peaks; original unchanged |
| warmup | {} | {ok:true, ready:true} — load the on-disk listening model once (after onboarding / app open, not on first drop) |
| history_state | {} | {canUndo, canRedo} — session stack in the Python process |
| undo | {} | {canUndo, canRedo} |
| redo | {} | {canUndo, canRedo} |

`destFolder` must be `Mixed` or a sanitized AudioSet class name. `resolve_library_file` requires a file under `libraryRoot`, but after a library-folder change it may re-home `ClassFolder/filename` onto the new root if that file exists.

## Electron

- `ipcMain.handle("python-call", (e, method, params) => pythonCall(method, params))`
- Promise map keyed by `id`. Bad stdout lines are logged, not fatal.
- Events: `webContents.send("python-event", msg)` — `progress` and `backend` (`ok` / `retrying` / `missing` / `dead`)
- preload: `window.fieldy.call`, `onEvent`, `pathForFile`, `statPath`, `chooseLibraryRoot`, `readPlaybackFile`, `startLibraryDrag`, `showInFinder`, `openExternal`, `retryPython`
- `app.setName("Fieldy")` before `whenReady`. Spawn bundled `python-runtime` when packaged (`process.resourcesPath`); unpackaged uses repo `.venv` unless `python-runtime` exists. `PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1`, `PYTHONPATH={root}/python`, `FIELDY_ROOT`, `FIELDY_YAMNET_DIR`. Override with `FIELDY_PYTHON` / `FIELDY_ROOT`. Missing interpreter or repeated crash → `backend` events to the renderer (in-app dialog/banner), not a pip/`showErrorBox` lecture. `retry-python` resets the crash counter and respawns.
- IPC `error` strings: `core.errors.explain`. Renderer `friendlyError` strips `Error invoking remote method 'python-call'` and unknown leftovers become one generic line.
- `npm run pack` (repo root): `scripts/prepare-pack-resources.sh` (relocatable `python-runtime`) then unsigned unpacked macOS `.app` (`electron/dist/mac-arm64/Fieldy.app` on Apple Silicon). `FIELDY_UNSIGNED=1` sets `mac.identity: null`. `npm run pack:win` builds unsigned Windows x64 (`electron/dist/win-unpacked`, zip `Fieldy-windows-x64.zip`) using `python-runtime-win` and `python.exe`. `npm run dist:mac` is the optional Developer ID DMG (`scripts/dist-mac.sh`). The script exits if the certificate or notary env vars are missing.
- If Python exits, reject in-flight promises and respawn unless the app is quitting.
- `contextIsolation: true`, `nodeIntegration: false`, `sandbox: true`.

## Security

Do not enable `nodeIntegration`. Validate paths in Python. Ingest moves into `libraryRoot` only. `read-playback-file` is restricted to `fieldy-play-*.wav` under the OS temp directory. `start-library-drag` and `show-in-finder` only accept existing WAV/AIFF/FLAC/MP3 files inside the pointer `libraryRoot` (originals, not playback temps). `open-external` only accepts `https://` URLs.

Root `package.json` `npm start` → `electron/`. Move-to `<select>` must set `color` (native select defaults to black on the dark UI).
